# Test: MCP and REST list an external plugin's command with the parameters of its -api rpc
#
# Question: when an external plugin brings a -cmd module whose `target` node
# points with ze:rpc at an rpc of the -api module it also brings, do MCP and
# REST list the command with that rpc's input leaf `name`, its two texts and
# required, in the shape a compiled-in command's rpc input gets, and does a
# call through each reach the plugin with a good value while the daemon
# refuses a value the leaf's type refuses before the plugin is asked?
# Why not a unit test: TestBuildParamMetaReadsAnExternalPluginsRPC and
# TestBuildCommandMetaGivesAPluginOnlyCommandItsRPCParameters prove the
# metadata source over a resolved set and over maps. Only a daemon proves the
# source reads the set boot published, the MCP tool and the REST description
# are built from it, and a call crosses to the forked plugin.
#
# What each surface shows, read from the producing code:
#   - MCP groups `show acme-monitor status` and `target` into one tool,
#     ze_show_acme_monitor (groupCommands, toolName), whose inputSchema holds
#     `action` and the typed rpc input leaf `name`, with `title` from its
#     ze:help and `description` from its description (addYANGParams), and
#     `name` required; with typed params no `arguments` property is added.
#     The compiled-in comparison is `system command help`, whose rpc input
#     leaf `name` (ze-system-api.yang) is listed on ze_system_command in the
#     same shape: type, title, description; asserted below exactly as
#     test/plugin/mcp-tools-list-argument-texts.ci asserts it. MCP carries no
#     length bound for either: a JSON Schema property holds no YANG length.
#   - the action enum's description carries each command's YANG summary
#     (commandModelHelp.texts), never the plugin's Stage 1 summary.
#   - a call writes `name <value>` after the action (dispatchGenerated,
#     command.WriteInvocation); the plugin answers the arguments it received.
#   - REST describes the command from the same source (commandMetaSource,
#     apiCommandLister), with the param's short-help.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-plugin-external-yang-at-startup AC-41 (owner ruling P-1: "yes,
#   like current internal plugin, the exact same way"), MCP and REST.
# PREVENTS: an external plugin's command listed on the API surfaces with no
#   parameters (buildCommandMeta gave a command only a plugin serves none).
# Not proven here: gRPC. Its command list reads the same commandMetaSource
#   (buildAPIEngine, cmd/ze/hub/api.go), and no generic gRPC client exists for
#   a .ci; the unit tests above cover that source.
#
# Method: test/plugin/external-yang-command-argument.ci's daemon with an MCP
# listener on $PORT2 and a REST listener on $PORT3. `le test mcp` is a
# quick-exit command, so its output span is exact; `wait-tool` polls
# tools/list until the plugin's tool is listed.

option=timeout:value=90s
option=env:var=ZE_CONFIG_DIR:value=.
option=env:var=XDG_DATA_HOME:value=.
option=env:var=ze.ssh.password:value=testpass

stdin=init-answers:terminator=EOF_INIT
admin
testpass
127.0.0.1
$PORT
EOF_INIT

stdin=mcp:terminator=EOF_MCP
wait-tool ze_show_acme_monitor
probe tools/list
probe tools/call {"name":"ze_show_acme_monitor","arguments":{"action":"target","name":"probe-b"}}
probe tools/call {"name":"ze_show_acme_monitor","arguments":{"action":"target","name":"this-name-is-far-too-long"}}
EOF_MCP

tmpfs=rest-target.json:terminator=EOF_REST
{"command":"show acme-monitor target","params":{"name":"probe-c"}}
EOF_REST

tmpfs=commands.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
system {
	authentication {
		# bcrypt cost-4 hash of "testpass".
		user admin {
			password "$2a$04$UlwuiuH82Unfsq.XEMPGJeDkXwbm3KW.nvVaVXOd/JeFK8VjMjrQO"
		}
	}
}
environment {
	ssh {
		enabled true
		server main {
			ip 127.0.0.1;
			port $PORT;
		}
	}
	mcp {
		enabled true;
		auth-mode none;
		server main {
			ip 127.0.0.1;
			port $PORT2;
		}
	}
	api-server {
		rest {
			enabled true;
			server main {
				ip 127.0.0.1;
				port $PORT3;
			}
		}
	}
}
plugin {
	external acme-monitor {
		run "le test fixture plugin/external-yang commands"
		encoder json
	}
}
acme-monitor {
	target probe-a
	interval 5
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze init:stdin=init-answers:exit=0
cmd=background:seq=2:exec=ze start commands.conf:name=daemon:ready=Ze running.
# A good value reaches the plugin from MCP and from REST; the refused one never.
expect=stderr:pattern=FIXTURE: external-yang command show acme-monitor target args=\[(name )?probe-b\]
expect=stderr:pattern=FIXTURE: external-yang command show acme-monitor target args=\[(name )?probe-c\]
reject=stderr:pattern=args=\[[^\]]*this-name-is-far-too-long
reject=stderr:pattern=ZE-OBSERVER-FAIL

cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=le test mcp --port $PORT2:stdin=mcp:timeout=30s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=probe status=200 code=ok
# The plugin's tool: action and the typed leaf name, required, no arguments.
expect=stdout:pattern="inputSchema":\{"properties":\{"action":\{[^}]*\},"name":\{"description":"The target name, from 1 to 16 characters\.","title":"Name of the target\.","type":"string"\}\},"required":\["action","name"\],"type":"object"\},"name":"ze_show_acme_monitor"
# The compiled-in comparison: the rpc input leaf of system command help.
expect=stdout:pattern="name":\{"description":"The full command name, as command-list prints it\. A name in\\nneither registry fails with unknown command\.","title":"Command name","type":"string"\}
# The YANG summaries name the actions, never the Stage 1 one.
expect=stdout:pattern=status: Show whether the acme monitor is polling\.
expect=stdout:pattern=target: Show one target the acme monitor polls\.
reject=stdout:contains=Declared at Stage 1, not in the YANG.
# The good call is the plugin's answer, with the value it received.
expect=stdout:pattern=\[(name )?probe-b\]
# The long value is the daemon's refusal of the leaf's length.
expect=stdout:contains=is outside the accepted length (25 characters)

# REST describes the command from the same source, then runs it. The config
# declares a user, so REST requires a credential on every request
# (buildAPIAuthentication, cmd/ze/hub/api.go: with users, `Bearer
# <user>:<password>`; RESTServer.withAuth answers 401 without one), as
# test/plugin/rest-peer-set-delete-lifecycle.ci sends its token.
http=wait:seq=1:url=http://127.0.0.1:$PORT3/api/v1/commands/show/acme-monitor/target:status=200:contains=Name of the target.:header=Authorization: Bearer admin:testpass:timeout=30s
http=post:seq=2:url=http://127.0.0.1:$PORT3/api/v1/execute:status=200:sendfile=rest-target.json:contains=probe-c:header=Authorization: Bearer admin:testpass
